entries.text:
{w=0.4}"That's fine by me, and I can confirm it: he's telling the truth."{w}

"The reason why I stayed on the fourth floor was different from everyone else's. It was because I quickly began to hear noise coming from the floor above me. More specifically, footsteps that I now know belonged to Katei."{w}

"I paid attention to see if there was anything I could figure out from them, but they simply kept going in circles, so it gave the impression that whoever was walking above me was either lost in thought or fairly nervous."{w}

"For most of the time, the sound of footsteps came directly from the third partition. However, during the last few minutes, they left it and started to come from outside the offices."{w}

"When I heard the elevator, I thought the person above me would come down. That never happened, though, and the footsteps never ceased. There was no time for Katei to do anything."

